":false,"isPrivate":false,"license":{"key":"","name":"","url":""},"updatedAt":"2025-07-23T14:37:14Z","url":"https://github.com/Ankesh-cloud/Simulation-of-Acid-Gas-Removal-Unit-using-ASPEN-HYSYS"},{"description":"The notebook featured in this repository takes data from some standard Aspen HYSYS reports and organizes it to enable analysis. Some exergy analysis and efficiency calculations are also conducted for a power plant.","fullName":"italosichi/HYSYS_data_import","isArchived":false,"isPrivate":false,"license":{"key":"","name":"","url":""},"updatedAt":"2023-10-17T13:10:04Z","url":"https://github.com/italosichi/HYSYS_data_import"},{"description":"Steady-state simulation of a natural gas sweetening unit using DEA solvent in Aspen HYSYS V14. Models full absorption-regeneration loop. >99.9% H₂S removal. Complete stream tables, column profiles, and energy analysis included.","fullName":"shahria-sunny/Natural-Gas-Sweetening","isArchived":false,"isPrivate":false,"license":{"key":"mit","name":"MIT License","url":"https://api.github.com/licenses/mit"},"updatedAt":"2026-05-03T16:19:16Z","url":"https://github.com/shahria-sunny/Natural-Gas-Sweetening"},{"description":"This project designs and evaluates the economic feasibility of a Hydrodealkylation (HDA) plant for toluene using MATLAB and Aspen HYSYS. It optimizes reactor conditions and process flows to determine the most viable operating parameters.","fullName":"SinaGhanbarii/HDA-Plant-Simulation","isArchived":false,"isPrivate":false,"license":{"key":"","name":"","url":""},"updatedAt":"2026-03-10T14:10:32Z","url":"https://github.com/SinaGhanbarii/HDA-Plant-Simulation"},{"description":"A comprehensive process simulation of crude oil characterization and fractionation using Aspen Hysys. The project models a pre-treatment unit and an atmospheric distillation column to separate crude oil into high-value products like kerosene, diesel, and AGO, demonstrating proficiency in process design, heat integration, and equipment sizing.",